dict(u=B,speaker='new_mother',stage='looking_back',type='belief',themes=['comparison_other_mothers','social_media','first_pregnancy'],quote="So many stories I see of women saying they were only in labour for 10-24 hours and then their baby was born, even for first babies. Or women saying their early labour wasn’t very painful and was sporadic, not at all like what I was experiencing.",context='Same post; measuring her labour against stories online.'),
dict(u=B,speaker='new_mother',stage='looking_back',type='tried_failed',themes=['birth_course','hypnobirthing','birth_prep'],quote="Because of all the reading and learning I had done on birth I believed this was the “rest and be thankful stage” before transition.",context='Same post; her preparation shaped how she read her own labour at home.'),
